"Pulse is the number of times your heart beats per minute (bpm). A normal resting heart rate for adults is typically between 60 and 100 bpm." = "脉搏是每分钟心跳次数（次/分）。成年人正常静息心率通常在 60 到 100 次/分之间。";
"Health Index combines your heart rate variability and pulse into a single 0–10 recovery score. Higher values suggest your body is well recovered." = "健康指数综合心率变异性和脉搏，得出 0–10 的恢复评分。数值越高，说明恢复越好。";
"Energy estimates how much recovery capacity you have, scaled from 0 to 120. It rises with higher heart rate variability." = "能量反映你的恢复能力，范围为 0–120。心率变异性越高，能量值越高。";
"Stress estimates your current allostatic load from 0 to 100. Lower values mean a more relaxed state; higher values suggest tension." = "压力反映当前 0–100 的累积负荷。数值越低越放松，越高越紧张。";
"HRV is the variation between consecutive heartbeats. It is a useful marker of recovery and stress." = "HRV 是连续心跳之间的时间变化，是恢复和压力的重要指标。";
"SDNN is the standard deviation of your NN intervals. It reflects overall variability across the measurement." = "SDNN 是 NN 间期的标准差，反映整段测量的整体变异性。";
"RMSSD is the root mean square of successive differences between NN intervals. It is the primary short-term HRV metric." = "RMSSD 是相邻 NN 间期差值的均方根，是主要的短期 HRV 指标。";
"pNN50 is the percentage of consecutive NN interval pairs that differ by more than 50 ms. It reflects parasympathetic activity." = "pNN50 是相邻 NN 间期差值超过 50 毫秒的比例，反映副交感神经活动。";
